---
import SiteLayout from "@/layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const models = [
  { name: "HUMAIN M3", acceptable: "56,202", total: "85,246", score: "65.93%" },
  {
    name: "MiniMax M3",
    acceptable: "54,969",
    total: "85,246",
    score: "64.48%",
  },
];
---

<SiteLayout
  title="HUMAIN M3 vs MiniMax M3 — Historical Najd Study"
  description="A historical pre-audit Najd Research comparison across 6,089 case IDs, 28 configurations, and 170,492 graded outputs."
>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="page-shell header-inner">
      <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="Najd Research home">
        <img
          class="wordmark-logo"
          src="/logo.webp"
          alt=""
          width="96"
          height="49"
        />
        <span>Najd Research</span>
      </a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary navigation">
        <a href="/">Home</a><a href="/research/humain-m3-vs-minimax-m3/"
          >Research</a
        >
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>
  <main id="main-content" class="page-shell report">
    <div class="report-kicker">Historical research / 2026.09</div>
    <h1>HUMAIN M3<br /><em>vs MiniMax M3.</em></h1>
    <p class="report-lead">
      A preserved Najd Research experiment compared the models across 6,089 case
      IDs and 14 configurations per model. The verified snapshot holds 170,492
      grades.
    </p>

    <section class="scores" aria-label="Full-denominator scores">
      {
        models.map(model => (
          <article class="model-card">
            <>
              <h2>{model.name}</h2>
              <strong>{model.score}</strong>
            </>
            <p>
              {model.acceptable} acceptable / {model.total} total outputs
            </p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </section>

    <aside class="disclosure">
      <strong>Historical pre-audit result.</strong> This run covers all 6,089 case
      IDs in the current Hugging Face release, including its 372 quarantined cases,
      but some case contents changed before publication. Historical evidence differs
      on 1,419 prompts and 1,422 expected answers. These figures are not an exact
      run of the current release or a certified Arena leaderboard ranking.
    </aside>

    <section class="report-section">
      <span class="section-number">01 / METHOD</span><h2>
        What the score means
      </h2>
      <p>
        “Correct” and “possible correct” count as acceptable. Every other
        outcome, including a technical failure, counts as zero. All 6,089 case
        IDs remain in the denominator for every configuration. The snapshot
        contains 170,367 usable grades and 125 technical failures. HUMAIN M3
        leads by 1.45 percentage points under this historical protocol.
      </p>
      <div class="facts">
        <div><strong>6,089</strong><span>case IDs</span></div><div>
          <strong>28</strong><span>configurations</span>
        </div><div><strong>170,492</strong><span>graded outputs</span></div><div
        >
          <strong>372</strong><span>quarantined case IDs</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-section">
      <span class="section-number">02 / EVIDENCE</span><h2>What was checked</h2>
      <p>
        The archive’s grade and evidence files matched their SHA-256 manifest.
        The import checked every case ID against the pinned Hugging Face release
        and found a complete 6,089-case set in each of 28 configurations. Only
        grades and audit metadata were imported into Arena. Raw model answers
        remain private.
      </p>
      <p>
        An <a
          href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1sxxj3zvP82EGQzcmmki_dSLruzEsQVG8/view"
          >earlier PDF report</a
        > used an older snapshot and has different figures. The current result above
        comes from the later verified snapshot. The PDF may require Drive access.
      </p>
      <div class="links">
        <a
          href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/najdresearch/najd-benchmark/tree/cb30c1c9e46c62f691380c3269885cdb8f22f52b"
          >Pinned dataset ↗</a
        ><a href="/research/historical-m3-results.md">Markdown report ↗</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-section">
      <span class="section-number">03 / NEXT TEST</span><h2>
        Exact-release comparison
      </h2>
      <p>
        A fresh run must use the published case contents. The 372 quarantined
        cases need suitable fixtures, repairs, or a stated handling rule before
        a new 6,089-case result can be called canonical.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer>
    <div class="page-shell report-footer">
      <a href="/">Najd Research</a><span>Historical study · September 2026</span
      >
    </div>
  </footer>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .report {
    padding-block: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 6rem) 7rem;
  }
  .report-kicker,
  .section-number {
    color: var(--green);
    font:
      650 0.72rem/1.4 "JetBrains Mono Variable",
      monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  h1 {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font:
      500 clamp(3.4rem, 8vw, 8rem)/0.95 "Newsreader Variable",
      serif;
    letter-spacing: -0.055em;
  }
  h1 em {
    color: var(--green);
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .report-lead {
    max-width: 49rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .scores {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  .model-card {
    padding: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 2.2rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: #ffffffa8;
  }
  .model-card h2 {
    font:
      650 0.72rem/1.4 "JetBrains Mono Variable",
      monospace;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .model-card strong {
    display: block;
    margin-block: 1.4rem 0.5rem;
    color: var(--green);
    font:
      500 clamp(3.7rem, 7vw, 6.2rem)/1 "Newsreader Variable",
      serif;
  }
  .model-card p {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font:
      0.77rem/1.5 "JetBrains Mono Variable",
      monospace;
  }
  .disclosure {
    max-width: 70rem;
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
    padding: 1.4rem 1.6rem;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--green);
    background: #006c3512;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .report-section {
    max-width: 75rem;
    margin-top: 5rem;
    padding-top: 1.4rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .report-section h2 {
    margin-block: 0.9rem 1.3rem;
    font:
      500 clamp(2.3rem, 5vw, 4rem)/1 "Newsreader Variable",
      serif;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }
  .report-section p {
    max-width: 54rem;
    margin-block: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .report-section a {
    color: var(--green);
  }
  .facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .facts div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.2rem;
    padding-top: 0.7rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .facts strong {
    font:
      500 clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.5rem)/1 "Newsreader Variable",
      serif;
  }
  .facts span {
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font:
      0.7rem/1.5 "JetBrains Mono Variable",
      monospace;
  }
  .links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font:
      650 0.76rem/1.4 "JetBrains Mono Variable",
      monospace;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .report-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-block: 2rem;
    font:
      0.75rem/1.5 "JetBrains Mono Variable",
      monospace;
  }
  .report-footer a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .scores {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .facts {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
</style>
